      "value": "@{65f4b1a3d0a7a0c657a7d3a8|full_name} A question I have: why would VRChat be using the listed fallback shader unless the particle shader was being blocked? Why does having a listed fallback shader cause the particle shaders to be blocked? Is there any way to manually remove the fallback option in the shader/material? \n\nWhen editing the multiply and additive via text editor, the tags section does not include the VRCFallback tag (image attached). Would the tag be attached to the .mat? I currently don't know how to open that file. \n\nI uploaded another test avtr_4391b7c2-fceb-4197-97f3-a807f692902b, and for this one I edited and saved the additive and multiply vrchat shaders with the added tag \"VRCFallback\"=\"Particle\" (2nd image attached). The in-game results are the same, but I wonder if the tag attached to the material/shader changed on your end? I assume you have more in-depth debug tools as a dev.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "_id": "693ae405248a1e235c63f148",
      "aiGenerated": false,
      "author": {
        "_id": "674414d25e7599ab848e8934",
        "alias": "Excellent Canid",
        "aliasID": "674414d3a367fa6392f003cc",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/8a1329990998ababdf01ca72a0c070b7.png",
        "created": "2024-11-25T06:10:26.750Z",
        "name": "Lilyyy6_",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5d09629c3511d825c8e56214",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2025-12-11T15:32:21.059Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "deletedAt": null,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "692c88553081d9c7ea120c22",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 3
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "FIX I FOUND A FIX AAAA\n\nOk, so usually when doing the quest version of the model, you would create a new project and change the shader of the pc material directly, or you would CTRL + D the material and then change the duplicate. I think by creating the material this way, it inherits some of the VRCFallback properties we don't want, because it makes the particle shaders not work. \n\nSo to fix this, simply right click in assets and do Create > Material. Then name your material. Then, change the shader to VRChat > Mobile > Particles > Multiply/Additive and add your texture. Using this new material that hasn't inherited any unwanted values, particles will again work on quest. :) \n\nI think everyone should test this method and see if it is a temporary fix while vrchat gets the game to not make particle shaders be blocked and fallback when there is a VRCFallback tag listed.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
